# Stop preview servers

When you start a local preview server for a task (`next dev`, `npm run dev`, `vite`, or similar), stop that process before you finish. Leave servers the user already had running.

Stop only the process you started. Use its pid from the terminal session. Do not kill an unrelated process that happens to share the port.

```bash
# GOOD — the dev server you launched
kill 36801

# BAD — a server that was already running when the task began
kill $(lsof -t -iTCP:3000)
```
